---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusPill from '../../components/StatusPill.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/siteUrl';
---

<Layout
  title="Image Treatments"
  description="Shape image and vector results with Varve's editable local texture, dehaze, vignette, grain, and highlight glow treatments."
>
  <div class="container-custom">
    <main class="feature-page">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href={sitePath('/features')}>Features</a> / Image Treatments
      </nav>

      <header class="page-hero">
        <StatusPill status="available" />
        <h1>Texture, depth, and finish without flattening the work.</h1>
        <p>
          Varve's Image Treatments are editable effects on the rendered result. Use them
          for photo adjustment or to give an otherwise flat vector object a considered,
          material finish while its original geometry and opacity stay intact.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="feature-section feature-section--grid" aria-labelledby="treatments-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">A focused toolkit</p>
          <h2 id="treatments-title">Use the name that describes the result.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="treatment-grid">
          <article><h3>Fine Texture</h3><p>Accentuate or soften fine surface detail while protecting smooth areas.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Local Contrast</h3><p>Separate medium-sized forms without relying on a global contrast slider.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Atmospheric Depth</h3><p>Shape broad local depth without mislabelling it as haze removal.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Dehaze</h3><p>Recover contrast through a distinct local atmospheric-veil model.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Vignette</h3><p>Darken or brighten object edges with controllable feather, shape, and centre.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Grain</h3><p>Control amount, size, roughness, and deterministic pattern variation.</p></article>
          <article><h3>Highlight Glow</h3><p>Turn bright or mid-tone areas into a soft, luminous halo.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">One underlying model</p>
          <h2 id="workflow-title">Choose a local filter or a scoped adjustment.</h2>
          <p>
            Image Tuning is the quick photo surface for selected images. Object Filters
            attach an ordered treatment stack to one rendered object. Adjustment Layers
            apply the same operators to a chosen scope and can use an adjustment mask.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline" aria-label="Image treatment attachment options">
          <div class="pipeline-step"><span>01</span><strong>Image Tuning</strong><small>Curated controls for images</small></div>
          <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="pipeline-step pipeline-step--accent"><span>02</span><strong>Object Filter</strong><small>One editable object</small></div>
          <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
          <div class="pipeline-step"><span>03</span><strong>Adjustment Layer</strong><small>Scoped objects or a mask</small></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="feature-section" aria-labelledby="vector-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">For vector work too</p>
        <h2 id="vector-title">Finish a gray rectangle without turning it into pixels.</h2>
        <p>
          Select the rectangle, open Appearance → Object Filters, then use Object Finishing
          to add Grain, Vignette, or Highlight Glow. A gray rectangle at 50% opacity remains
          a gray rectangle at 50% opacity; the treatment is an editable node-local filter on
          its rendered result. The complete Object Filter menu also retains the photo-local
          operators when you explicitly want them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <aside class="honesty" aria-labelledby="honesty-title">
        <h2 id="honesty-title">Clear names, honest boundaries.</h2>
        <p>
          Atmospheric Depth and Dehaze are not aliases. The first shapes broad local depth;
          the second estimates atmospheric veil. Treatments preserve source alpha, remain
          non-destructive, and use the shared canvas and export compositor rather than a
          CSS-only preview.
        </p>
        <a href={sitePath('/docs/tools/image-treatments')}>Read the Image Treatments guide →</a>
      </aside>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .feature-page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 0 5rem; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .875rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .page-hero { max-width: 710px; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .page-hero h1 { color: var(--text-primary); font: 700 clamp(2.3rem, 6vw, 4rem)/1.05 var(--font-editorial); letter-spacing: -.025em; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .page-hero p, .feature-section p, .honesty p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .feature-section { margin: 0 0 4rem; }
  .feature-section h2, .honesty h2 { color: var(--text-primary); font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.3rem); margin: .5rem 0 1rem; }
  .treatment-grid { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: 1.75rem; }
  .treatment-grid article { border-top: 2px solid var(--border-accent); padding-top: 1rem; }
  .treatment-grid h3 { color: var(--text-primary); margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .treatment-grid p { font-size: .95rem; margin: 0; }
  .workflow, .honesty { background: var(--surface-card); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: 1rem; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .pipeline { align-items: stretch; display: grid; gap: .75rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .pipeline-step { border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: .7rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .45rem; padding: 1rem; }
  .pipeline-step--accent { background: var(--surface-accent-soft); border-color: var(--border-accent); }
  .pipeline-step span { color: var(--text-tertiary); font-size: .7rem; }
  .pipeline-step strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .pipeline-step small { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.4; }
  .pipeline-arrow { align-self: center; color: var(--accent-primary); font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .honesty a { color: var(--text-link); font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .treatment-grid, .pipeline { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .pipeline-arrow { justify-self: center; transform: rotate(90deg); } }
</style>
